    "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nThe doctor and status commands display warnings about multiple remotes when they detect ambiguous checkpoint destinations. However, these warnings were shown even when the user had explicitly configured a checkpoint_push_remote setting, making the warning confusing and redundant.\nSolution:\nThe code now checks whether a checkpoint remote was explicitly selected via the checkpoint_push_remote configuration setting before deciding to show ambiguity warnings. If an explicit selection exists, the multi-remote choice warning is suppressed—though a warning about multiple push URLs on that specific remote is still shown if applicable.\nThe fix adds a new explicitlySelected field to track this state and uses it to gate the ambiguity checks in two places: the ambiguous() method and the describeCheckpointDestination() output formatter. Tests verify that explicit selections suppress the choice warning while preserving warnings about multiple URLs and allowing the warning to appear when no explicit configuration is set.",
